###########################################################
# WGS Bioinformatics Pipeline Final Notes
# Last updated: June 2026

## Overview
Whole genome sequencing pipeline for Culex pipiens complex population genetics.
65 samples input, 52 samples retained after QC filtering in R,
281,262 final SNPs (thinned) used for PCA and FST analyses.
Reference genome: Cpip29_nodeb_gfill_mito.fasta (unpublished, stored on CHPC)

## Software versions
- BWA-MEM2 v2.2.1
- samtools v1.16
- bcftools v1.23
- GATK [version TBD]
- vcftools [version TBD]
- FastQC v0.12.1
- MultiQC v1.12
- Python 3.6+

## Sample information
- 65 total samples across 7 populations
- Libraries prepared by Andrea Gloria-Soria at Connecticut Agricultural Experiment Station
- Sequencing platform: Illumina Nova-Seq X 
- Target: ~40 million reads per sample, ≥15x non-repetitive coverage
- Read length: 150 bp paired-end
- Mean coverage achieved: ~14x (range 1.1x-40.6x)

## Population sample sizes (pre/post filtering)
| Population | Pre-filter | Post-filter | Dropped |
|---|---|---|---|
| Box Elder (BE) | 4 | 3 | 1 |
| Cache | 5 | 5 | 0 |
| Salt Lake (SLC) | 13 | 10 | 3 |
| Southwest (SGE) | 6 | 5 | 1 |
| Utah County (UTCO) | 18 | 14 | 4 |
| Weber (OGD) | 5 | 5 | 0 |
| West Millard (WMAD) | 14 | 10 | 4 |
| Total | 65 | 52 | 13 |

## Pipeline steps

### 1. FastQC (1a_fastqc.slurm)
- Per-sample read quality assessment
- Runs as SLURM job array (one job per FASTQ file)
- Input: raw FASTQ files in Cx_WGS_raw/
- Output: per-sample .html reports in fastQC_WGS_Cx/

### 1b. MultiQC (1b_multiqc.slurm)
- Aggregates all FastQC reports into single summary
- Output: multiqc_report.html in fastQC_WGS_Cx/multiqc/
- NOTE: No trimming performed - FastQC/MultiQC results
  deemed acceptable to proceed directly to alignment

### 2. BWA-MEM2 alignment (2_bwamem-alignrefs.slurm + 2b_bwa_mem.pl)
- Paired-end alignment to Cpip29_nodeb_gfill_mito.fasta reference
- Perl wrapper runs 4 samples in parallel (4 jobs x 2 threads each)
- Flags: -M (mark split alignments)
- Skips samples with existing BAM (safe to resubmit if job dies)
- NOTE: No read groups added — compatible with bcftools variant
  caller but would need to be added for GATK HaplotypeCaller
- Output: per-sample sorted BAMs in Cx_WGS_bwa/

### 3. Merge lanes (3_mergebams.slurm)
- Merges per-lane BAMs into per-sample BAMs
- Samples with single lane are copied directly
- Creates mergedbam_list.txt for downstream array jobs
- Input: Cx_WGS_bwa/ (lane-level BAMs)
- Output: Cx_WGS_mergedbams/ (sample-level BAMs)

### 4. Mark duplicates (4_markdups.slurm)
- Runs as SLURM job array (one job per sample)
- Six-step samtools pipeline:
  1. Name sort
  2. fixmate -m (adds mc tag for markdup)
  3. Coordinate sort
  4. markdup (marks but does NOT remove duplicates)
  5. Index
  6. flagstat QC
- Intermediate files cleaned up automatically
- Output: per-sample .markdup.bam + .flagstat.txt in Cx_WGS_final/

### 4. Flagstat summary (4b_flagstat_summary.py)
- Python script aggregating per-sample flagstat files
- Extracts: total reads, mapped reads, mapping%, duplicate count, dup%
- Output: mergedflagstat_summary_clean.txt in Cx_WGS_finalbams/
- NOTE: file is in Cx_WGS_finalbams/ not Cx_WGS_final/

### 5. Coverage summary (5-rdeptable.py  + runner script)
- Python script computing weighted mean depth per sample
- Uses samtools coverage, weights by scaffold length
- Output: mergedcoverage_summary.txt in Cx_WGS_finalbams/
- NOTE: file is in Cx_WGS_finalbams/ not Cx_WGS_final/

### 6. Variant calling - Stage 1 (6_bcftools_call.slurm)
- Joint variant calling across all 65 samples simultaneously
- bcftools mpileup | bcftools call pipeline
- Filters applied during calling:
  - --min-BQ 30 (minimum base quality)
  - --min-MQ 30 (minimum mapping quality)
  - --max-depth 100 (per sample depth cap)
  - Duplicates skipped (default bcftools behavior)
- --multiallelic-caller model, --variants-only
- Output: Culex_final_variants.vcf.gz (69,238,059 SNPs, 65 samples)

### 7. Bias filtering - Stage 2 (7_gatk_bias_filter.slurm)
- Uses GATK VariantFiltration ONLY for bias Z-score filters
- NOT used for variant calling (no read groups required)
- Three bias filters applied (|Z| <= 3 threshold):
  - BQBZ: base quality bias
  - MQBZ: mapping quality bias
  - RPBZ: read position bias
- Requires bgzip recompression for GATK compatibility
- Only PASS variants retained after filtering
- Output: Culex_stage2_bias_filtered.vcf.gz (39,132,169 SNPs)

### 8. Population filtering + thinning - Stage 3 (7b_vcftools_stage3.slurm)
- vcftools filters applied:
  - --max-missing 0.80 (≥80% genotyping rate per locus)
  - --mac 3 (minimum minor allele count)
  - --min-alleles 2 --max-alleles 2 (biallelic only)
  - --remove-indels (SNPs only)
  - --thin 1000 (1 SNP per 1000bp window for LD reduction)
- Output: Culex_WGS_65samp_stage3_thinned.vcf.gz (281,262 SNPs)

### Downstream analyses (R)
- PCA, FST computed in R on 281,262 SNP thinned dataset
- 13 low quality samples removed in R based on PCA outlier status
  leaving 52 samples for final analyses
- ADMIXTURE on WGS-only dataset: NOT YET RUN (as of June 2026)
- Scripts in: [R script directory TBD]

## Key numbers summary
| Step | Filter | SNPs | Samples |
|---|---|---|---|
| Stage 1 - bcftools calling | MQ≥30, BQ≥30, MaxDP=100 | 69,238,059 | 65 |
| Stage 2 - GATK bias filter | BQBZ/MQBZ/RPBZ \|Z\|≤3 | 39,132,169 | 65 |
| Stage 3 - vcftools + thin | missing≤20%, MAC≥3, thin 1000bp | 281,262 | 65 |
| Final (post R QC) | PCA outlier removal | 281,262 | 52 |

